# Tool permissions shared by every Copilot agent run by .claude/scripts/macos/run-agent.sh.
# One flag per line. The runner refuses --allow-all*, interpreters (bash, sh, perl, python, node, env…)
# and anything that is not a flag. Unlisted shell commands are denied (runs are non-interactive).
# The only shell command an agent may run is the gateway (.github/copilot/gateway.conf): analyze, test,
# format, pub get and read-only git. Reading and searching use Copilot's built-in tools, not the shell.
# Agents never touch git history. The governor (Claude) commits only when the owner has authorised it for the cycle (feature.md rule 5).
--allow-tool=shell(.github/copilot/scripts/macos/gateway.sh:*)
--deny-tool=shell(git:*)
--deny-tool=shell(gh:*)
--deny-tool=shell(rm -rf:*)
--deny-tool=shell(rm -r:*)
# Pipeline, agent and project-instruction files are the owner's, never an agent's.
--deny-tool=write(.claude/**)
--deny-tool=write(.github/**)
--deny-tool=write(CLAUDE.md)
